{%- comment -%}
  lb-content-visibility.liquid
  Version:      1.1.0
  Last updated: 2026-05-20

  Purpose:
    Applies content-visibility: auto to below-the-fold sections so the
    browser skips paint and layout for off-screen content until it
    approaches the viewport, reducing initial render time.

  Changes v1.1.0:
    - contain-intrinsic-size raised from 600px → 900px. 600px was a
      rough guess that underestimated typical section heights (product
      grids, hero-like media sections) causing visible scrollbar jump
      as sections painted and the layout shrank from the guessed height
      to actual height. 900px is a closer midpoint for the section mix
      on this store. The 'auto' prefix means the browser caches the
      real height after first paint so subsequent scrolls have zero jank.
    - Added explicit content-visibility: visible overrides for the
      announcement bar (.header-section, aside[class*="announcement"]).
      Previously the announcement bar could receive content-visibility:
      auto if Shopify section ordering placed it as a non-first child,
      hiding it until the viewport reached it — which on some browsers
      caused the bar to flash in on load. Announcement bar is above the
      fold by definition, so it must always be visible.
    - Added [data-sticky] and .sticky-content overrides for completeness.

  Targets: .shopify-section that is NOT the first section in the page.
  Safe list: header group, footer, announcement bar, sticky elements.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  /* Skip rendering for off-screen sections — browser recalculates on scroll.
     'auto 900px' = browser uses cached real height after first paint,
     falls back to 900px placeholder before first paint to prevent CLS. */
  .shopify-section:not(:first-child) {
    content-visibility: auto;
    contain-intrinsic-size: auto 900px;
  }

  /* Never apply to header, footer, announcement bar, or sticky elements.
     These are either above the fold or must remain layout-present at all times. */
  #header-group .shopify-section,
  footer .shopify-section,
  aside.announcement-bar,
  aside[class*="announcement"],
  .header-section,
  [data-sticky],
  .sticky-content,
  .sticky-content--desktop {
    content-visibility: visible;
    contain-intrinsic-size: none;
  }
</style>
